FINAL ANSWER:
**Bus factor of `lib/`: 2 by commit count. By current line ownership, it is already 0.**

**By commits** (66 commits, 25 authors, merges excluded):
- Troy Goode has 33 commits (50%). Alejandro Caravaca Puchades and Douglas Christopher Wilson have 4 each (6.1%).
- The tool defines bus factor as the fewest authors who together cover more than 50% of commits. Troy has exactly 50%, so it takes Troy plus one more author to pass that line.
- If Troy and one other author left, the people who remain would hold less than half of the commit history.
- `lib/` is not flagged as a knowledge silo. The silo rule needs one author above 80%, and no one is close.

**By who owns the code today** (blame at HEAD):
- `lib/` has one file, `lib/index.js`, with 238 lines. The tool marks it as orphaned.
- "Inactive" means no commit since 2026-04-22.
- Fiona Formatter owns 214 lines (89.9%). Their last commit was 2026-04-12, so they count as inactive.
- Troy Goode owns 20 lines (8.4%) and is also inactive, with a last commit on 2026-04-10.
- Raymond Feng (last commit 2015) owns 2 lines. Douglas Christopher Wilson (last commit 2021) and Eric di Domenico (last commit 2013) own 1 line each.
- Inactive authors own 100% of the lines.

**Caveats:**
- Fiona Formatter is probably a formatter or bot identity. It likely comes from the latest commit, `style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes`. That commit rewrote nearly every line, so blame credits those lines to it instead of to the people who wrote the logic.
- The tool's 90% orphaned figure is therefore misleading. To see who understands the code, I'd re-run blame while ignoring that commit (`git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0`). The commit-count view above is the better guide until then.
- Troy Goode appears inactive by the 6-month cutoff, even though they have the most commits. So the practical position is that the largest source of knowledge has already left. The remaining contributors each wrote only a few commits.

I can re-run the ownership analysis with the reformat commit ignored if you want.

